// kaleidoscope-tavern.jsonl in Minecraft 1.20.1's NBT, for 1.20.1 (Refabricated) and 1.20.1-forge (the
// official mod): items carry the thirstwastaken2 compound rather than components, and items are matched
// with nbt selectors. Everything else, the header below included, is that script's; run it with this file's
// name in place of the other's.
//
// Kaleidoscope Tavern in a real client: water keeps its grade through the barrel, two grades poured
// together keep the worse, sea water is refused by the barrel and the shaker, a tap copies a Dirty
// cauldron's grade and samples a waterlogged slab in the sea, a water bottle the tap fills keeps its
// grade when broken, and a sea-water bottle shift-placed and picked up again comes back salty. It runs
// on every node with the integration, 1.21.1-neoforge and the Fabric ones from 1.21.1 on; 1.20.1 has its
// own copy in that version's NBT. Run it unattended in a singleplayer world:
//     ./gradlew ":<node>:runClient" -Pagent=tools/agent/integrations/kaleidoscope-tavern.jsonl -Pquickplay=TavernAgent
// TavernAgent is a throwaway world, made fresh for each run by
//     python tools/agent/new_world.py <node> TavernAgent
// Then check what it recorded:
//     python tools/agent/drive.py run/<node>/agent/client tools/agent/integrations/kaleidoscope-tavern.jsonl --verify --max-age 15
// Every "execute" line checks that it said "Test passed", and the captures in
// run/<node>/agent/client/screenshots/ show Jade's line beside a barrel of Dirty water, looked at from a
// side block with no block entity of its own, and on the salty cauldron a tap filled.
//
// canteenRefused passes only on Fabric, where Refabricated's barrel would hand a canteen back as a
// bucket and so refuses it; on NeoForge the canteen goes in, and that line is the only one that may fail.
//
// The barrel is three blocks a side, placed by the player like any block, with its one block entity at
// the bottom centre (0 200 0) and its lid at the top centre (0 202 0), which takes containers while it
// is open, as it is when placed. The lid is clicked by standing on it and looking straight down. Each
// tap is opened by a redstone block above it. A grade is stored on the barrel as one int,
// thirstwastaken2:water_quality: 1 to 4 for Dirty, Murky, Clean and Pure, 5 for sea water, as a cauldron
// stores it in its purity property.

{"id": "load", "command": "wait", "args": {"ticks": 400}}
{"id": "arrived", "command": "client.state"}
{"id": "survival", "command": "server.command", "args": {"command": "gamemode survival @p"}}
